			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_568174730608310925">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475851404', '582809103434380736', '568174730608300015', '102508710', '568174730608310925' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_568174730608310925">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568174730608310796">Thomzen</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568174730608309463">Fear57</a></b>:</div>Fact buddy. Its here and its going nowhere. You are the person laughing at the clown on stage who is saying the building is on fire. </blockquote>Saying &quot;it is going nowhere&quot; is such a defeatist statement. Gamers have the power to choose what games they buy. If games developed with AI don't get any sales and &quot;regular&quot; games do then game developers will eventually stop using AI. In the end the consumer has the choice to vote with their wallet </blockquote>Do you tell developers to code in 0s and 1s instead of programming languages that make it easier to program? Are they dumb because they don't do it the &quot;true&quot; way? The same reaction happened when we invented phonograph (canned music!), cameras (painting is the only true art!), electricity, internet, cars...<br><br>If humanity had waited for people like you to give them permission to innovate, the world would be so boring. Oh, and we'll all be dead by now without any technologies if we feared used them. All of them are dual use, we exploit the good, minimize the bad.<br><br>AI coding and asset generation literally enables indie developers to do passion projects and what used to require millions of dollars and expensive dev teams. It literally democratizes art and access to infinite entertainment for everyone. You should be complaining about the low effort generic human slop that triple A companies do every year, instead of moaning about the golden age of gaming and modding that is coming thanks to new technologies.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div class="forum_audit">
			Last edited by <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/id/Raulikien" class="hoverunderline">Raulikien</a>;
